# const back = input(function () {}); back.constructor; back()
# `Function` is the `constructor` of every function, so whoever holds a function holds it. That a closure has escaped, and that `constructor` is read off a value nobody knows, says no more than that:
# only `Function` itself in unknown hands, or a call of it, is an event.
